# Auto-generated by `pnpm choibot setup`; the server refuses this example value.
CONSOLE_COOKIE_SECRET=at-least-32-chars-of-random-secret-here
# Root directory the agents and editor operate on.
WORKSPACE_DIR=/home/you/workspace
# Console listen port. HOST=127.0.0.1 keeps it loopback-only; remote access runs over Tailscale (`tailscale serve`).
PORT=3100
HOST=127.0.0.1
CODE_SERVER_BIND=127.0.0.1:8081
# A console behind a front proxy (a hosted one): the proxy's address. Written by `first-start`; with the four below, a private TLS listener runs on this server's one address in the network, for the proxy only. Unset = off.
# CONSOLE_PROXY_FROM=10.0.0.2
# The private network of the front proxy (an RFC 1918 range).
# CONSOLE_PROXY_NETWORK=10.0.0.0/16
# The port of the private listener.
# CONSOLE_PROXY_PORT=3443
# The SHA-256 of the proxy's token for this console (the proxy alone keeps the token).
# CONSOLE_PROXY_TOKEN_SHA256=<64 hex>
# key.pem and cert.pem of the private listener (0600), made by `first-start`.
# CONSOLE_PROXY_TLS_DIR=/home/you/.local/share/choibot/chief/proxy-tls
# Cron data (job specs, run results, the retired cron master's memory). Default: ~/.local/share/choibot/cron.
# CRON_DATA_DIR=/home/you/.local/share/choibot/cron
# Issues tab data (issues, photos, Telegram poll offset). Default: ~/.local/share/choibot/issues.
# ISSUES_DATA_DIR=/home/you/.local/share/choibot/issues
# Fleet master home (agent cwd, memory). Default: ~/.local/share/choibot/master.
# MASTER_DATA_DIR=/home/you/.local/share/choibot/master
# Agent widgets (one folder per agent and widget). Default: .widgets-data in the console dir.
# WIDGETS_DATA_DIR=/home/you/workspace/choibot/.widgets-data
# Claude account new agents use when none is chosen (an account id from the launcher). Unset = the box's default login.
# CLAUDE_DEFAULT_ACCOUNT=work
# Set to 0 to turn off the prompt card's screen reader (one headless terminal per live agent).
# AGENT_PROMPT_WATCH=0
# Keys of this env that agents also get, comma-separated. Set (also empty): agents get only what they need to run plus these keys. Unset: every key. The console's secrets never reach agents.
# AGENT_ENV_PASS=MY_DB_URL,MY_API_KEY
# More places that the Files tab of the Server page never shows (it already hides keys, logins and .env files): absolute paths with ":" between them.
# FILES_REFUSED_EXTRA=/srv/private:/opt/backups
# The share tool of "Share outside" on a ticket (set it in Settings): one program that takes scan, add and remove (README, Share outside). Unset: a ticket page can only be downloaded.
# SHARE_TOOL=/home/you/bin/share-tool
# 1 = the console's own GitHub calls use the ChoiBot GitHub app's token (repos that you pick), once you connect it. Off by default; the agents' own gh login does not change.
# GITHUB_APP_LOGIN=1
# The client id of the ChoiBot GitHub app (a public value, not a secret). Needed with GITHUB_APP_LOGIN=1.
# GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID=<the app's client id>
# The public page of the ChoiBot GitHub app. The Set-up page links to it, to install the app on the repos that you pick.
# GITHUB_APP_URL=https://github.com/apps/choibot
# Written by setup with the resolved dtach path.
# AGENT_DTACH_BIN=/usr/bin/dtach
# Written by setup with the resolved claude path.
# CLAUDE_CODE_EXECUTABLE=/home/you/.local/bin/claude
# Written by setup with the resolved codex path. Optional — only needed for Codex agents.
# CODEX_EXECUTABLE=/home/you/.nvm/versions/node/v24/bin/codex
# Optional agent-finished notifications (bot from @BotFather).
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=your-notification-bot-token
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=your-chat-id
# Set to 0 to keep Telegram for cron job results only (agent status pings stay in-app).
# TELEGRAM_NOTIFY_AGENTS=0
# Forum group for cron results (with TELEGRAM_CRON_THREAD_ID). Unset = TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID.
# TELEGRAM_CRON_CHAT_ID=-1001234567890
# Topic id (message_thread_id) for cron results in TELEGRAM_CRON_CHAT_ID.
# TELEGRAM_CRON_THREAD_ID=4
# The only Telegram user id allowed to send issues to the bot (private chat). Unset = issue intake off.
# TELEGRAM_ISSUES_USER_ID=123456789
# 0/false = deprecated private-chat issue intake off (forward issues to the Master topic). Card replies still work.
# TELEGRAM_ISSUE_INTAKE=0
# Forum group (negative id) for the fleet master. Needs TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN and TELEGRAM_ISSUES_USER_ID; the bot must be a group admin.
# TELEGRAM_MASTER_CHAT_ID=-1001234567890
# message_thread_id of the Master topic (not General). The console logs `[master] seen forum message chat=… thread=…` while unset.
# TELEGRAM_MASTER_THREAD_ID=2
# Unset = off. 1 turns on the chief of staff (brain, decision queue, lead agents).
# CHIEF_ENABLED=1
# Chief data dir. Default: $XDG_DATA_HOME/choibot/chief.
# CHIEF_DATA_DIR=/home/you/.local/share/choibot/chief
# Public origin for pairing links. Required when CHIEF_ENABLED=1; doctor fails without it.
# CHIEF_CONSOLE_URL=https://console.your-tailnet.ts.net
# Uid agents must run as for strong mode. Never turns strong mode on by itself.
# CHIEF_AGENT_UID=1001
# sudo used to run agents as CHIEF_AGENT_UID (hardened deployment only).
# AGENT_SUDO_BIN=/usr/bin/sudo
# The installed deploy/choibot-agent-exec (hardened deployment only).
# AGENT_EXEC_HELPER=/usr/local/bin/choibot-agent-exec
# Root of the fleet master and lead homes, and of the retired cron master's memory (hardened deployment only): root-owned, group choibot, mode 3770; the console makes the homes. Absolute, no symlink in it.
# AGENT_HOME_ROOT=/srv/choibot-agent-homes
# The agents' own Claude config dir (choibot-agent's login). Required in a hardened deployment, never the console's own CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR.
# AGENT_CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/home/choibot-agent/.claude
# Strong protection only: the uid of the second account, which runs the fleet master, the leads and the Coordinator (the workers cannot read their tokens). Unset = one account for all agents. strong-setup writes it.
# CHIEF_PERSISTENT_UID=1002
# With CHIEF_PERSISTENT_UID: the second account's own Claude config dir (its own sign-in; never a copy of the workers').
# AGENT_CHIEF_CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/home/choibot-chief/.claude
# With CHIEF_PERSISTENT_UID: the second account's own dtach dir (the console's, its group, 3770; never AGENT_DTACH_DIR).
# AGENT_CHIEF_DTACH_DIR=/run/choibot-dtach-chief
# How devices pair. telegram (default): through the Master topic, which must be configured. log: from the server; a Master topic is optional there.
# CHIEF_USER_AUTH=telegram
# Auto-answer confidence threshold.
# CHIEF_AUTO_THRESHOLD=0.85
# Undo window for auto-answers, in minutes.
# CHIEF_UNDO_MINUTES=10
# Daily distill time (host timezone).
# CHIEF_DISTILL_AT=03:30
# Set to 0 to silence auto-answer one-liners in Telegram.
# CHIEF_TELEGRAM_AUTO=1
# 1: the CLI refuses port 3100 and requires PORT. For tests only.
# CHIEF_TEST=1
# The systemd user unit the console runs in (default choibot.service; choibot.service on an install with the old names). The deploy ticket restarts only this unit.
# CHIEF_DEPLOY_UNIT=choibot.service
